🔐 (Optional) Securing HTTP Cron Routes:
If you want to protect the /cron/* web URLs with a secret token, add this to your .env file:

env
CRON_SECRET=your_secret_token_here
And append ?key=your_secret_token_here to your curl URL:

bash
* * * * * curl -s "https://files.ashishkumar.info/cron/run?key=your_secret_token_here" >/dev/null 2>&1
🩺 Health Check URL:
You can check current cron health and status anytime by visiting:

https://files.ashishkumar.info/cron/status
